 ## Overview
-VoxelGrid Down Sample reduces the resolution of a voxel grid representation, typically by a factor of 2, to generate lower-resolution levels of a multi-resolution hierarchy. It addresses the problem of managing memory and computational cost in volume rendering by creating coarser approximations of the scene geometry or density. It differs from sibling methods like [Morphological Pyramid](1641-morphological-pyramid.md) by often employing specific hardware-accelerated compute kernels (e.g., in GPU shaders) that combine repacking with upsampling logic, or by using max-pooling for feature reduction, whereas [Mipmap Generation](2602-mipmap-generation.md) typically focuses on texture filtering.
+VoxelGrid Down Sample reduces the resolution of a voxel grid representation to generate lower-resolution levels of a multi-resolution hierarchy [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It addresses memory and computational cost constraints in volume rendering by creating coarser approximations of scene geometry or density [S3, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods like [Morphological Pyramid](1641-morphological-pyramid.md) by employing hardware-accelerated compute kernels that combine repacking with upsampling logic, or by using max-pooling for feature reduction, whereas [Mipmap Generation](2602-mipmap-generation.md) typically focuses on texture filtering [S2, unofficial][S4, unofficial].
 
